# Requires Python and the standard-library statistics module.
Use the Python library called statistics as stats.

Let weekly_ticket_counts be [42, 47, 51, 45, 55].
Say "Weekly average: {stats.mean(weekly_ticket_counts)} tickets.".
Say "Population standard deviation: {stats.pstdev(weekly_ticket_counts)} tickets.".
Say "Named-argument average: {stats.fmean(data=weekly_ticket_counts)} tickets.".
